<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Drŭĭdes</span></b> , um
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Drŭĭdae</span></b> ,
			ārum, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1,
		41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 14, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 4,
		54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
		451</span></i>.—Dub. form acc. Druidas, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 2,
		3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 30, 1, 4, § 13</span></i>),
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				Druids</i>, <i>the priests and wise men of the
				Gauls</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 6, 13 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1</span></i>.
			1.; <i><span class="en">Plin.
				16, 44, 95, § 249</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Drŭïas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>a
				Gallic priestess and prophetess</i>, <i>a
			Druidess</i>, <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev.
			60</span></i>.—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Drŭis</span></b> , ĭdis,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2200</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 44</span></i>; Numer.
		15.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
